# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# The ignore list the publishing host's sync folder carries.
#
# 🚨 **This is the sync-layer half of the publish boundary, and it is belt to the server's
# suspenders — both wear it.** The server refuses to serve anything outside its publish
# boundary even if this file were empty; this file is what keeps the internal material
# from ever *arriving* on a machine whose only job is to be public. Two independent
# enforcement points, because the consequences are asymmetric: the boundary refusing at
# serve time is one bug away from a leak; the bytes never landing is not a bug away from
# anything.
#
# ⚠️ **Keep this file and the boundary's defaults in step.** The boundary decides what the
# *server* will serve; this decides what the *folder* will hold. If you widen one and not
# the other, the wider one is your true boundary — write that down rather than discovering
# it in a log.
#
# Syntax: Syncthing's ignore patterns (https://docs.syncthing.net/users/ignoring), one
# per line. `(?d)` marks a pattern safe to delete files over — everything here is, because
# nothing on this machine is authoritative.

// The publish boundary's excluded roots.
(?d)/Internal Wiki
(?d)/90-99 Agents
// 00-09 Metafiles: everything except the public task root (which publishes).
(?d)/00-09 Metafiles/*
!/00-09 Metafiles/01 Tasks
(?d)/00-09 Metafiles/01 Tasks/*
!/00-09 Metafiles/01 Tasks/Templates

// Obsidian's own machinery — nothing in a .obsidian directory belongs on a public server.
(?d)/.obsidian
(?d)/.trash

// Sync machinery, if the authoring side carries it.
(?d)/.stfolder
(?d)/.stversions

// The base files the allowlist does not name. The server would refuse them anyway;
// not syncing them is the cleaner statement.
(?d)/*.base
!/Anthers Tasks.base